      "writtenOn": "2020-06-23T11:01:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Oh sorry I missed that bit. I would argue that we don\u0027t care about the capping here -- schedutil_cpu_util() does the capping anyway. And we don\u0027t have that capping upstream either (https://elixir.bootlin.com/linux/latest/source/kernel/sched/cpufreq_schedutil.c#L295) so I would suggest that we stick to the upstream version.\n\nQais: would you mind if we reverted to using cpu_util_cfs() here?",
      "parentUuid": "e1579e86_5a076b5e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 335,
        "startChar": 26,
        "endLine": 335,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "c41988f1f09aa71ff49d42a6e37a14c46fbf9fd1",
